4. PATENT NOTICE
----------------
The architecture implemented in this repository is the subject of the
following patent APPLICATIONS. No patent has yet been granted, and no
enforceable patent right exists in any jurisdiction until grant.

  - Turkish national patent application TR 2025/012696
    (filed 4 September 2025)
  - International application PCT/IB2026/053070
    (filed 27 March 2026, claiming the above priority)

Status of examination:

  - The TÜRKPATENT search report for the national application cited no
    document in category X (a document that alone prejudices novelty).
  - International search under the PCT has been carried out by the
    European Patent Office. The European Patent Office found the
    subject-matter of several claims — including the split-window
    running-sum computation, the Guardian sideband and the array
    architecture — to be new over the cited art, and raised objections
    against the remaining claims. The international search report and
    written opinion will be published together with the application
    and may be consulted by any interested party at that time.
  - Examination in the national and regional phases is ongoing. Claim
    scope may change during examination.

The claims as currently pursued are directed to a specific hardware
arrangement: a decision derived from the difference between values
representing two successive intervals of a sample window, maintained
by running sums at a cost independent of window depth, compared
without reference to the absolute magnitude of any individual sample,
and applied to alter the element's own hardware operating mode
without any processor, program counter, instruction memory, state
machine or centralised control unit in the decision path.

The claims are drafted independently of hardware description language
and process node.


